1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,500
AI can generate software faster than we understand it.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Does what we build leave our teams more free?

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,300
Generation is cheap.

4
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:15,400
Understanding and owning what we build still takes judgment.

5
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:18,000
AI speeds whichever loop we feed.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Faster output can become a heavier burden.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,500
A lesson from Toyota: build human learning into the work.

8
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:30,000
“The list must not be empty.”

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Turn that known rule into a check.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,500
An empty list fails. Further work stops.

11
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:42,000
People investigate the cause, fix it, and improve the check.

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
The next person need not rediscover the rule.

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,500
People keep the authority to improve that check.

14
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:54,000
Free attention for discovery. Customer value still needs judgment.

15
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Start with a real customer need: get home after dinner.

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Deliver one useful result: the next train leaves at 22:45.

17
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,800
“Does that route have stairs?”

18
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:15,000
Keep the train result. A step-free route is next.

19
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Leave later work unstarted.

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Use that freedom to learn together.

21
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Give capable people responsibility and support.

22
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,300
Build products that free people.

23
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:31,000
Trust them with the next real problem.
